spec ww08-different-properties-one-node: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW08. s1 writes n.a, s2 writes n.b — different properties of ONE node. The node is
# the unit of conflict (F4), so the second writer is refused, the same verdict as
# PostgreSQL's and InnoDB's row granularity. A narrowing of the conflict unit to
# per-property would show here as a diff.

starting permutation: s1w s1c s2w s2c
step s1w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.a = 1 RETURN n.a AS a
a
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.b = 2 RETURN n.b AS b
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n.a AS a, n.b AS b
a|b
-+-
1|0
(1 row)

